            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Most of what I reported is intended behavior, as it turns out. I hadn't realized that in/out brackets behave differently as *input* these modes (I'm pretty sure that only mattered for *output* in `vim-surround`, which is my reference point).\r\n\r\nIt also looks like getting tag deletion to remove empty lines and detent surrounded ones is just a matter of setting `respect_selection_type`.",
